{"text": " You wake up today in Nairobi. Matatou's honk on the road outside and your phone buzzes. Your sister just sent you money from a village far up country. It took seconds. Did you know that about eight and 10 adults in Kenya now use mobile money? In 2009, it was under three and 10. MPs launched here in 2007. You hand cash to a shopkeeper and it turns into numbers on your phone, school fees and taxi rides get paid with a text. And it isn't just Kenya. Across the Euro area, cash paid for about eight and 10 shop purchases in 2016. By 2024, it was about half. So what is money to you? Numbers on a screen. You almost never touch it. So here's the question you came for. If it isn't paper and it isn't gold, what is money actually?", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 1.88, "text": " You wake up today in Nairobi.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 965, 294, 50205, 20027, 13, 50500], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010282572577982, "compression_ratio": 1.5410958904109588, "no_speech_prob": 0.03423352539539337, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.14, "probability": 0.646588921546936}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.14, "end": 0.3, "probability": 0.9579348564147949}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.3, "end": 0.44, "probability": 0.9986264705657959}, {"word": " today", "start": 0.44, "end": 0.72, "probability": 0.9953922033309937}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.72, "end": 1.44, "probability": 0.8459553122520447}, {"word": " Nairobi.", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.88, "probability": 0.995885968208313}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.8, "end": 5.36, "text": " Matatou's honk on the road outside and your phone buzzes.", "tokens": [50500, 6789, 267, 263, 311, 2157, 74, 322, 264, 3060, 2380, 293, 428, 2593, 13036, 279, 13, 50660], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15010282572577982, "compression_ratio": 1.5410958904109588, "no_speech_prob": 0.03423352539539337, "words": [{"word": " Matatou's", "start": 2.8, "end": 3.28, "probability": 0.549117